+# Receipts stopped
+
+For the volunteer on call when members report no receipt emails. Gets the worker sending receipts again. Written
+after members went without receipts twice in September 2024 because the deploy script does not restart the worker,
+and the second time a volunteer with no background waited until noon. Owner: whoever is on call.
+
+## Before you begin
+
+- SSH access to the host running `larder-worker`, and `psql` access to the `larder` database.
+
+## Steps
+
+1. Check the worker.
+
+       systemctl status larder-worker
+
+   Expected: `active (running)`. If it says `inactive (dead)`, that is the cause: a deploy restarts the web app but
+   not the worker, so the worker stays dead until someone starts it.
+2. Count the queued jobs.
+
+       psql larder -c "select status, count(*) from procrastinate_jobs group by status"
+
+   Expected: a non-zero `todo` count (the backlog built up while the worker was down) and little or nothing `doing`.
+3. Start the worker.
+
+       sudo systemctl start larder-worker
+4. Run the same query from step 2 every minute or so and watch `todo` fall to 0. A few `failed` rows are normal and
+   not the problem here: those are typically bounced emails for members with no valid address.
+
+## If it fails
+
+If the worker goes back to `inactive (dead)` right after starting, it is crashing on something other than the deploy
+not restarting it: run `journalctl -u larder-worker -n 50` to see why, and ask in the pantry's chat (#larder-ops).
